  "mechanism": [
    "The numbers support candidate (a): the flux read and the current placement are inconsistent. The discrete Green's coupling and the boundary flux interpolant were tuned to chord moments, so feeding the map exact cut-cell moments solves a different problem than the one the flux read was balanced against.",
    "Armed exact participation without the two contaminated boundary cells (arm b) converges to a self-consistent fixed point of the discrete map (residual 6.2e-13, converged True) - but it is a different equilibrium: its magnetic axis sits 0.533 m outboard of the analytic axis while the chord control's axis is within 1.8 mm, and its contour panel shows a smooth equilibrium that is not the reference Solov'ev one.",
    "Including the two contaminated cells (cells 101 and 102) prevents even that self-consistent fixed point: the exact-arm terminal residual stays at 0.4708 (63.2x the banked chord residual), unqualified, never converged. Two-cell contamination is therefore a secondary effect layered on the primary flux-read/current-placement inconsistency.",
    "Step damping was not measured: the relaxation selector is inert for the certificate route (arm c), so the damping candidate (c) is unadjudicated."
  ],
